WEBVTT

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:23.800
Jeez, I hate the rain!

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:25.180
My hair gets super frizzy

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:26.330
When it's humid out...

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.040
Huh? But your hair looks nice like always.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:30.780
It's not too bad yet.

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:32.150
I've got it under control

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:33.250
For the time being.

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:34.680
Are you serious?

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:36.790
What happens when it gets out of control?

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:40.460
How'd you do that?!

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.630
Well, I guess I can't blame 
you for hating the rain...

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:49.500
You wanna hear a story that
might make you like it instead?

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:56.210
It's one of the Seven Wonders of
Karai High School: "The Umbrella of Love."

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:01.170
They say that if you walk home with someone
under the same umbrella on a rainy day,

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:03.040
you'll be together forever.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:07.460
Whatcha think? You like the rain now?

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:08.990
Oh, I love the rain!

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.320
After all, my skin feels soft

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:11.500
When it's humid out!

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:18.000
Sorry, Nanako-chan...
I just wanted to see you smile...

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.290
I made the whole thing up.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:24.460
Gentle words

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:27.580
Soft feelings

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:32.500
Precious memories

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:39.030
They're dyed with love

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:45.330
When I'm with you, even getting caught
in the rain turns into something new

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:48.540
What words can I string together

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:51.670
To keep this color from fading away?

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:53.250
I know

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:59.170
What the two of us will 
become on that far-off day

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:04.580
Isn't that right, God?

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:08.100
Waiting for the train, the 
water droplets beading up

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:10.670
I really wish this moment

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:15.670
Could somehow last forever

00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:17.710
Is that too much to ask?

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:26.000
Poem 7: Nanako and the 
Seven Wonders of the Rain

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:41.750
Whoa, Busujima-kun's soaking wet!

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:44.210
Didn't you know? Thugs like 
him don't use umbrellas.

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:45.290
Wait, for real?

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:47.310
Oh my gosh, Ei-chan!

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:48.810
You're going to catch a cold!

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:50.060
Here, use my towel!

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:51.670
Thank you!

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:54.960
I have an umbrella in my bag, but I don't 
bother unless it starts comin' down hard.

00:02:56.210 --> 00:02:57.880
It is coming down hard...

00:02:58.540 --> 00:02:59.580
An umbrella?

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:04.580
If you both bring one, just pretend you 
forgot yours or lost it or whatever.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:06.040
Then you can share his!

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:11.290
What's wrong, Nanako?

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:16.900
I was just thinking...

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:18.250
We should walk home together.

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:19.460
That okay with you?

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:21.250
Huh? Sure.

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:24.500
Oh good, the rain finally let up!

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:30.580
What's the matter, Nanako?

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:32.780
Oh no, it's nothing!

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:34.010
Just thinking about some stuff...

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:34.940
Laundry and all that!

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:37.130
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:03.460
Hey, Yukishiro!

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:06.420
You're on the Clean-up Committee, aren't you?

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:11.040
It looks like yesterday's typhoon made
a mess of the rabbit hutch.

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:13.830
You mind helping with the repairs?

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:17.800
Only problem is, several 
students are claiming that

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:20.560
a "monster" has taken up 
residence near the hutch...

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:30.750
Whaddya want?!

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:33.040
Come to help me fix this thing?

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:36.710
You know what, Ei-chan?

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:38.070
Taking care of animals

00:04:38.070 --> 00:04:39.000
Suits you pretty well!

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:43.630
Think so? Well, I do like 'em...

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:47.420
Isn't this awful?

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:51.710
I managed to move all the rabbits somewhere
safe though, so they should be okay.

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:55.830
Those ears remind me

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:57.310
Of all the fun we had at

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.710
The amusement park!

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:01.710
I-I don't know what you're talking about!

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:03.540
I'm just trying to blend in!

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:08.290
The rabbits get scared and take off runnin'
whenever they see me.

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:10.790
I wear these so they don't freak out.

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:16.290
But man, we pretty much gotta
rebuild the whole thing...

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:18.750
What are you two love birds-

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:20.000
What are you doing?

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:22.920
Hey, Tao. Just takin' care 
of some committee stuff.

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:24.590
Oh, that reminds me!

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:25.760
Are you on a committee

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:26.880
Of some sort, Tao-chan?

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:29.000
I'm kind of on the Newspaper Committee...

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:32.670
Great! You can run a story 
about the new hutch!

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:36.460
Sure, not a problem. As for the headline...

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:56.460
Local man ruins everything!!!!

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:51.130
This is my prediction.

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:53.710
Don't use fortune telling 
as a basis for journalism!

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:56.000
And how did I manage to 
screw it up that badly?!

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:57.210
See you later.

00:05:57.210 --> 00:06:00.920
Y-you can't just leave!
Help us keep your prediction from coming true!

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:03.380
I guess I've got no choice...

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:09.250
Cooperating with the boy in
the bunny ears will bring good fortune...

00:06:09.790 --> 00:06:14.350
I see. How about we start by moving
the broken branches?

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:15.330
Yeah!

00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:25.500
Next patient, please!

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:27.130
Crap, she's here!

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:28.820
Oh my, it's Eiji!

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:31.950
What's the matter? In need 
of some sex education?

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:33.830
God, no! Please don't!

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:35.630
I just need you to pull out some splinters!

00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:37.910
Ooh! "Pull out," hm?

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:41.170
Okie-dokie! Go ahead and lie down on the bed.

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:42.750
How would I even do that?!

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:47.210
Kino?

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:48.590
Kino-chan is on

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:49.760
The Clean-up Committee, too.

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:50.940
She's here to help out!

00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:51.960
Hiya!

00:06:52.750 --> 00:06:53.680
Glad to have you!

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:55.460
Let's get started!

00:06:58.630 --> 00:07:00.540
What kinda avant-garde monstrosity is that?!

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:01.250
Heh-heh!

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:03.420
Our job is to keep

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:04.860
The campus grounds looking nice,

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:05.860
But this is too much!

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:07.790
You really think so?

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:12.540
I'm not sure the rabbits will
be very comfortable in there...

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:13.830
Probably not...

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:23.380
Hare House

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:23.380
Whew... Finally done!

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:25.040
We really did it.

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:26.330
Come to think of it,

00:07:26.330 --> 00:07:27.620
It's actually pretty fun

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:28.670
Building stuff outdoors!

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:29.630
Yup!

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:33.750
They're makin' themselves right at home, too.

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:38.270
Wow, it's finished!

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:41.420
You guys actually built this? It's amazing!

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:45.750
Well, it's not that big a 
deal. Take a look inside.

00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:49.170
I'd say THAT'S a pretty big deal!

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:51.860
No way! The door fell off its hinges?!

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:54.380
Just as I thought. My 
prediction wasn't off at all.

00:07:54.380 --> 00:07:56.460
C'mon, we gotta catch 'em quick!

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:02.290
This is an announcement from
the Student Broadcasting Committee.

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:07.500
Ten rabbits have escaped from 
the outdoor rabbit hutch.

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:11.830
We ask for your cooperation in their capture.

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:17.490
In the event you catch one, we 
request that you bring it back to

00:08:13.830 --> 00:08:16.580
H-how'd they find out so fast...?

00:08:17.420 --> 00:08:19.640
Wait a second, I know that voice...!

00:08:17.490 --> 00:08:19.640
the rabbit hutch as soon as possible.

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:25.210
That is all. This has been an announcement
from the Student Broadcasting Committee.

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:26.540
President?!

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:35.630
Hare House

00:08:32.350 --> 00:08:33.460
Thanks!

00:08:36.170 --> 00:08:38.080
Well then, I'll be on my way.

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:39.210
Later!

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:41.580
Yeah, thanks a ton!

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:44.000
I'm gonna feed these little 
guys before headin' out!

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:51.750
What's wrong, Nanako?

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:56.460
Don't you remember?!

00:08:56.460 --> 00:08:57.940
You promised me that we would

00:08:57.940 --> 00:08:59.050
Walk home together...

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:01.580
Oh, right! Sorry 'bout that!

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:03.570
How about you gimme a hand?

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:09.920
Yes...!

00:09:13.710 --> 00:09:16.910
Oh man... It started raining again...

00:09:17.420 --> 00:09:20.580
We're pretty much done with everything, so...
we should probably head home.

00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:26.260
This is terrible!

00:09:26.260 --> 00:09:27.700
I forgot my umbrella.

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:28.880
I can't believe it...

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:31.590
You wanna use mine?

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:38.420
My bad... Looks like I didn't
bring it with me after all.

00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:40.460
Wanna use this instead?

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:43.460
Should keep you dry enough.

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:55.070
Jeez, did you BOTH forget 
your umbrellas today?

00:09:55.070 --> 00:09:57.990
Oh, President! Thanks for makin'
that announcement earlier.

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:00.630
Here, you can borrow mine.

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:02.500
But if we do that,

00:10:02.500 --> 00:10:04.100
You won't have an umbrella.

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:05.080
You're gonna get wet!

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:09.170
No worries! I carry a spare just in case
something like this happens.

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:12.210
Good luck!

00:10:24.130 --> 00:10:25.490
I guess there's no choice...

00:10:25.970 --> 00:10:27.490
We only have the one, so...

00:10:27.790 --> 00:10:29.290
We'll have to share it.

00:10:30.750 --> 00:10:32.830
Y-yeah...

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:41.040
W-wait... Isn't there a word for this...?

00:10:41.880 --> 00:10:43.670
Well... doesn't matter.

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:49.330
You're more invested in their love lives
than your own, aren't you?

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:53.580
Nah... Well, maybe just a little bit.

00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:57.540
You just can't help but 
want to cheer them on, huh?

00:11:10.130 --> 00:11:15.540
It's almost funny how different we are

00:11:15.710 --> 00:11:20.920
Down to our reflections in the shop window

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:26.580
When you smile as brightly as the sun

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:35.130
A peaceful feeling washes over me

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:42.330
Even my trivial, everyday life

00:11:42.330 --> 00:11:47.920
Begins to shine when I'm with you

00:11:47.920 --> 00:11:51.380
Even if something happened

00:11:51.380 --> 00:11:54.540
Even if we hurt each other sometimes

00:11:54.540 --> 00:12:01.880
Believe in our ordinary days

00:12:05.170 --> 00:12:06.530
On the next epi-

00:12:06.530 --> 00:12:07.790
-sode of Senryu Girl:

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:08.980
If Nanako Wore...

00:12:08.980 --> 00:12:10.650
...a Swimsuit!

00:12:12.170 --> 00:12:13.960
Next Time, Poem 8
"If Nanako Wore a Swimsuit"
